  "result": "Perfect! All 216 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the credit notes system:\n\n**Created src/credits.js with createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers):**\n- Returns ok(creditNote) with { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n- Generates credit note numbers with format CN-<year>-<counter> (separate counter from invoices)\n- Errors:\n  - NOT_ISSUED for draft invoices (only issued/partially_paid/paid allowed)\n  - DATE_INVALID for invalid date format\n  - AMOUNT_INVALID for non-positive or non-integer amounts\n  - CREDIT_TOO_HIGH if amount exceeds invoice total (after VAT, discount, and voucher)\n- Does not mutate the invoice\n\n**Added nextCreditNoteNumber() to src/numbering.js:**\n- Generates CN-<year>-<counter> format with separate counter per year\n- Tracks both invoice and credit note numbers (existingNumbers contains both types)\n- Counter resets each year\n\n**Added error code CREDIT_TOO_HIGH to src/errors.js**\n\n**Added 20 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Basic credit note creation with all fields\n- Status filtering (rejects draft, accepts issued/partially_paid/paid)\n- Date validation (invalid format)\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, fractional)\n- Amount limits (can't exceed invoice total)\n- Respects invoice VAT, discounts, and vouchers in total calculation\n- Separate numbering from invoices\n- Counter incrementing and yearly reset\n- Input immutability\n- Multiple line items\n- Edge cases (amount equals total, custom reasons)\n\nAll 216 tests passing.",
